For equally likely outcomes, the probability of an event $A$ is
\[
  P(A)=\frac{|A|}{|\Omega|}.
\]

For example, when rolling a fair six-sided die, the probability of rolling
an even number is
\[
  P(\text{even})=\frac{3}{6}=\frac{1}{2}.
\]

For events $A$ and $B$, the addition rule is
\[
  P(A\cup B)=P(A)+P(B)-P(A\cap B).
\]

